 change together: read the session's names from the VM, and sort before printing.
 `tests/repl_test.rs:repl_shows_the_result_of_an_expression_under_vars` pins the
 current `_` behaviour deliberately, so that phase has a red test to start from.
 
+**The ordering half is fixed after review.** `Repl::variable_lines` sorts the names
+before printing, so `:vars` gives the same listing for the same bindings in every
+session. The other half is still open: `Repl::execute_code` still records only `_`,
+so `:vars` still shows the last result rather than the session's names. That is
+the same root cause as #1 — the analyzer is seeded from one line at a time, so a
+`set` the session made is not a name the next line can read — and it should be
+fixed with it rather than beside it.
+
 ## 3. A stray `end` leaves the REPL stuck in continuation mode — `src/repl/mod.rs`
 
 The multi-line detector is a suffix heuristic (`src/repl/mod.rs:210`):
 a line opens a block if it ends with `then`/`end`/`to`/`else`/`while`/`repeat`.

