All seven findings are fixed and the four gates are green.

## Fixes

| # | Finding | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **BLOCKER** `:load` never ran anything | `load_file` now runs the source through `execute_code`, so the file's declarations become the session's own — the difference from `:run`, which uses a throwaway VM. `src/repl/mod.rs:343` |
| 2 | History load truncated silently | `map_while(Result::ok)` → `let line = line?`. `src/repl/history.rs:80` |
| 3 | `:vars` printed a `HashMap` in iteration order | `variable_lines` sorts before printing. `src/repl/mod.rs:308` |
| 4 | EOF dropped an unclosed block | `report_unclosed_block` prints the buffered lines and says they were never closed. `src/repl/mod.rs:239` |
| 5 | Command arguments kept one word | All six argument-taking commands read `parts[1..].join(" ")`; the alias table now asserts the argument, not just the variant. `src/repl/commands.rs:47` |
| 6 | `user_names` scanned only `globals` | Local scopes unioned in, so a `to`-defined function is offered. `src/vm.rs:426` |
| 7 | Multiline matched a line's last word | New `parser::open_block_depth(&tokens)`, counted from the token stream. `src/parser.rs:2021` |

Finding 7's counter needs two things the old heuristic had no notion of: an opener counts only at a statement boundary (so `for each i from 1 to 10` and `import MathUtils to M` are not unclosed bodies), and `else`/`catch`/`finally` are branches rather than statements (so `else if x then` still opens a block).

## Verification

I confirmed each fix is load-bearing by reverting it individually and watching the new tests fail — e.g. removing the `sort()` fails 10/10 runs, restoring the last-word heuristic fails 6 tests, and `:load` reverting to print-only fails 2.

Gates, re-run by me: `fmt --check` clean · `clippy --all-targets -D warnings` clean with no `allow(` added · `cargo test --all-targets` **813 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored** (was 785) · `cargo test --doc` 1 passed. No test deleted, no assertion weakened, no suppression added.

One thing worth flagging: `edge_a_decoded_chunk_runs_identically_to_the_compiled_one` failed once mid-session. It scans `examples/`, `modules/` and `tests/` for `.rb` files, and I had left a scratch file in one of those directories. It never reproduced in 8 isolated runs or 6 full-suite runs after cleanup, and nothing in this change writes there — but it is a real coupling between that test and the repo tree that this round did not address. Noted in `phases/phase-033/REPORT.md`.
